<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Inbound support tickets for the SupportTriageAgent example (LOB use case 1).
  Each <email> becomes an InboundMessage on the blackboard; the driver runs
  triage for every ticket. The <internal> element is metadata for the reader
  (what each scenario is meant to exercise) - the loader ignores it and only
  reads <channel>, <subject> and <body>.

  Tones span friendly / neutral / impatient; complexity and length vary; the
  set deliberately covers both terminal outcomes (escalate vs draft+route)
  across billing / technical / account / general categories.
-->
<emails>

  <!-- 1 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Impatient / angry billing dispute (double charge, no refund). High urgency, strongly negative sentiment - should trip the escalation gate.</internal>
    <channel>email</channel>
    <subject>Refund still not received</subject>
    <body>I was charged twice three weeks ago and STILL have no refund. This is completely unacceptable and I want it fixed today.</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 2 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Friendly, low-complexity billing question. Neutral/positive sentiment - billing-support queue, low urgency, no escalation.</internal>
    <channel>chat</channel>
    <subject>How do I export my invoices</subject>
    <body>Hi, could you tell me where I can download my past invoices? Thanks for the help.</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 3 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Neutral technical login problem, medium complexity. tech-support queue, normal urgency, no escalation.</internal>
    <channel>phone</channel>
    <subject>Cannot log in to my account</subject>
    <body>I have tried resetting my password twice but I still cannot sign in. The page just reloads without any message. Could you let me know what to check next?</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 4 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Friendly account-change request requiring identity verification. account-management queue, normal urgency, no escalation.</internal>
    <channel>email</channel>
    <subject>Please update the email on my account</subject>
    <body>Hello, I recently changed jobs and would like to update the email address on my account from my old one to my new one. What do you need from me to do this safely? Thank you.</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 5 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Neutral general inquiry, very low complexity and length. general-support queue, low urgency.</internal>
    <channel>web-form</channel>
    <subject>What are your support hours</subject>
    <body>Quick question - what are your support hours, and do you offer weekend coverage?</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 6 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Impatient critical outage, short and blunt. Urgency critical should trip the escalation gate even before sentiment is considered.</internal>
    <channel>chat</channel>
    <subject>API DOWN - we are losing money</subject>
    <body>Your API has been returning errors for the last 40 minutes and our checkout is completely broken. This is costing us real money. Fix it now.</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 7 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Friendly but long, multi-part, high-complexity technical integration question. tech-support queue, normal urgency, no escalation despite length.</internal>
    <channel>email</channel>
    <subject>Questions about the reporting API integration</subject>
    <body>Hi team, we are building an integration against your reporting API and I have a few questions. First, what is the rate limit per API key, and does it reset per minute or per hour? Second, the pagination cursor in the docs is described as opaque - is it safe to store it for more than 24 hours? Third, when a report is still generating the endpoint returns a 202 - should we poll the same URL or a separate status endpoint? Finally, are webhook retries idempotent, and which header should we use to deduplicate them? Appreciate the help, no rush.</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 8 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Neutral billing invoice discrepancy, medium complexity. billing-support queue, normal urgency, no escalation.</internal>
    <channel>email</channel>
    <subject>Invoice total does not match my plan</subject>
    <body>I am on the Team plan at the advertised monthly price, but my latest invoice is higher than expected and there is a line item I do not recognize. Could you help me understand the difference?</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 9 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Frustrated repeat contact, locked-out account, time pressure. Negative sentiment plus account issue - escalation likely.</internal>
    <channel>phone</channel>
    <subject>Third time asking - still locked out</subject>
    <body>This is the third time I am contacting you about being locked out of my account. Each time I am told it will be resolved and it never is. I need access today - I have a client presentation in two hours.</body>
  </email>

  <!-- 10 -->
  <email>
    <internal>Positive / friendly feedback with a minor feature question. Positive sentiment - routine routing, no escalation.</internal>
    <channel>chat</channel>
    <subject>Just wanted to say thanks</subject>
    <body>Just wanted to say the new dashboard is fantastic and saved my team a lot of time. One small thing - is there a way to set it as my default landing page? Either way, great work.</body>
  </email>

</emails>